<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phocaeans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Phocaeans were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionian Greeks</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, famed seafarers who explored the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. They founded Massalia (Marseille) around 600 BCE and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalia">Alalia</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a>, and traded with Tartessos in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>. Around 540 BCE they fought a Carthaginian and Etruscan fleet, including ships from Caere, off Alalia, after which they abandoned Corsica.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phocaeans.jpg" alt="Phocaeans" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: QuartierLatin1968 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_theatre_Fo%C3%A7a525.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
